    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: f2cc7ac5010e305b0ca73bbb8cf25938137f96c4 -->\nReview at head f2cc7ac50. Read, not built: the PR is from a fork, so its code does not run on the maintainer's runners, and no local build slot was free. The parent #3092 merged, so this reads against current main cleanly (base main, 6 files, +78).\n\nThe change reads well:\n- The template states only what the cited source gives (AGIE technical data C2.1, June 2002, sections 1.1 and 5.2 - a published vendor handbook). Travel endpoints, guide planes and conditions are left to the installer, and the description says so. Wire sizes 0.20 to 0.33 match section 5.2 per the test pin.\n- Registration is complete: the MACHINES list, the embedded include arm, and the shipped-machines count pin in `machine.rs`. The vendor string \"Camcraft\" follows the template convention (real machines carry their vendor).\n- `agiecut_template_refuses_a_wire_job_without_an_installed_condition` proves the safe default: the template refuses by name and creates no NC. The library test pins the axes, rapids, U/V travel and the empty EDM fields.\n- `docs/decisions/2946-agiecut-classic-2s.md` is in the PR. Body has `Changelog:` and `Fixes #2946`, and names what was not exercised (physical travel and cutting).\n\nClean. Labels: merge-ready; the P6 of issue #2946 stands on the PR.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
